  "root_cause": "The bug is caused by api.update_product calling both writer_a.write_fresh and writer_b.write_cached. write_cached (in writer_b.py) writes a cached value without updating the version, so when update_product calls write_cached after write_fresh it can overwrite the fresh, versioned write with a stale, unversioned value.",
  "code_commitments": [
    "update_product must call only write_fresh and not call write_cached",
    "api.py must not import write_cached"
  ],
  "fix_strategy": "Remove the redundant writer call by updating code_snippets_v2/overdetermination/api.py to import and call only write_fresh. This prevents the unversioned cached write from overwriting the fresh, versioned value.",
